From: Langsdorff <131063968+clangsdorff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 23:21:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] audiopolicy: treat hidl mix ports as routable

Dynamic profiles only get a device added to their routable list when
getAudioMixPort() succeeds, but the HIDL implementation returns
BAD_VALUE without an opened stream. USB headsets on HIDL vendors are
never routable, so no track can be created on the USB output.

Skip the query when the profile has no HAL port id, as routesToDevice()
already does for HIDL.
---
 services/audiopolicy/managerdefault/AudioPolicyManager.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/services/audiopolicy/managerdefault/AudioPolicyManager.cpp b/services/audiopolicy/managerdefault/AudioPolicyManager.cpp
index 2af1286..eeb006a 100644
--- a/services/audiopolicy/managerdefault/AudioPolicyManager.cpp
+++ b/services/audiopolicy/managerdefault/AudioPolicyManager.cpp
@@ -202,6 +202,7 @@ void AudioPolicyManager::addRoutableDeviceToProfiles(const sp<DeviceDescriptor>
                 !profile->hasDynamicAudioProfile() ||
                 !com::android::media::audioserver::enable_strict_port_routing_checks() ||
                 !com::android::media::audio::check_route_in_get_audio_mix_port() ||
+                profile->getHalId() == AUDIO_PORT_HANDLE_NONE ||
                 mpClientInterface->getAudioMixPort(&devicePort, &mixPort,
                                                    profile->getHalId()) == OK;
 
